{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>לשבת</b> — twice in the Masorah: here and the other: אשר נטה לשבת ער. One who married a woman and remained with her 10 years and she did not give birth — that is לשבת ער — he marries another. And the dwelling of ח\"ל does not count toward the tally, as written: לשבת אברם בארץ כנען. Meaning: when he dwelt ער in the land of Canaan."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The abbreviation ח\"ל is resolved here as חוץ לארץ (outside the Land); the argument links the two Masorah occurrences of לשבת to the halakhic rule about years of childless marriage counting only within the Land of Israel."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:14.158310781Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}